{
  "id": "swap-nodes-in-pairs",
  "questionId": "swap-nodes-in-pairs",
  "slug": "swap-nodes-in-pairs",
  "title": "Swap Nodes in Pairs",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Fast slow pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "fast & slow pointers",
    "linked list",
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "swapping values by index is straightforward with an array - the more interesting version of this problem is doing it by relinking actual next pointers, which is what the fast/slow style two-pointer walk is practicing",
    "keep a pointer to the node just before the current pair, so you can relink it to point at the second node of the pair once swapped",
    "for each pair, rewire: prev -> second -> first -> (rest of the list), then advance prev to what is now the end of this pair (the first node)",
    "handle the leftover single node at the end (if the list length is odd) by simply leaving it linked as-is when there's no second node to pair it with"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "losing the reference to the rest of the list while relinking a pair, breaking the chain",
    "not leaving a trailing unpaired node in place on odd-length lists",
    "swapping values in place with a temp variable when the point of the exercise is pointer manipulation (works for this problem's I/O, but doesn't build the intended skill)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A singly linked list is given to you as an array `nums`, where `nums[i]` is the value of the i-th node in order.\n\n**Swap every two adjacent nodes' values and return the resulting list's values in order.**\n\nIf the list has an odd number of nodes, leave the final unpaired node in place.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 100",
      "the number of nodes may be odd or even"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an empty list",
      "a single-node list",
      "an odd-length list where the last node is left unpaired"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]",
        "output": "[2, 1, 4, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2, 1, 4, 3]",
        "explanation": "swap (1,2) and (3,4)"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3]",
        "output": "[2, 1, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2, 1, 3]",
        "explanation": "swap (1,2), the trailing node 3 has no pair so it stays put"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = []",
        "output": "[]",
        "expectedOutput": "[]",
        "explanation": "an empty list has nothing to swap"
